.TH NEXIX 7 Nexix
.SH NAME
nexix \- native manual-reading and port notes
.SH DESCRIPTION
Nexix 0.2.0 ports the V7 distribution to x86_64.
Original manual sources are preserved unchanged in sections 0 through 8.
Presence of a manual does not imply that every documented command or interface
is implemented yet. The repository task list and inventory record port status.
.PP
The system uses ELF64 executables, native drivers and native ABI structures.
Historical header excerpts under /usr/man/include are documentation;
use /usr/include for native development.
Filesystem access, modification and change timestamps retain V7 semantics.
The kernel initializes UTC epoch time from RTC; libc applies the configured TZ.
.SH READING MANUALS
Use man name or man section name.
The default text pager supports space/b for forward/backward pages, j/k or
arrow keys for lines, Page Up/Down, g/G for beginning/end, /text and ?text for
literal search, n/N to repeat/reverse, and q to quit.
Redirected manual output contains no pager controls.
MANPAGER overrides PAGER; the default is more.
.PP
The original formatter modes are retained: -n uses nroff, -ne uses terminal
equation processing, -t uses troff, -e uses eqn and troff, and -w lists source
paths. Historical -k/-ek modes emit Tektronix graphics and are not keyword search.
.SH SEE ALSO
man(1), more(1), ps(1), uptime(1)
